    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "[Followup from Sourceforge Tracker]",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Followup Submitter: sjw46",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Logged In: YES ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "user_id=1709161",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Originator: YES",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "After running an install and selecting Postgresql, the first attempt to start",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Fedora 2.2 results in the following error:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "**************************",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "content": [
           {
            "type": "paragraph"
           },
           {
            "content": [
             {
              "content": [
               {
                "content": [
                 {
                  "text": "FEDORA STARTUP ERROR **",
                  "type": "text"
                 },
                 {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                 },
                 {
                  "text": "**************************",
                  "type": "text"
                 }
                ],
                "type": "paragraph"
               }
              ],
              "type": "listItem"
             }
            ],
            "type": "bulletList"
           }
          ],
          "type": "listItem"
         }
        ],
        "type": "bulletList"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Fedora startup failed",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "fedora.server.errors.ModuleInitializationException: A connection pool could not",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "be instantiated. The underlying error was a java.lang.NumberFormatExceptionThe",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "message was \"null\".",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "at",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "fedora.server.storage.ConnectionPoolManagerImpl.initModule(ConnectionPoolManagerImpl.java:214)",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "at fedora.server.Module.<init>(Module.java:48)",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "at",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "fedora.server.storage.ConnectionPoolManagerImpl.<init>(ConnectionPoolManagerImpl.java:69)",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "------- Additional Comment #1 From Chris Wilper 2007-01-23 12:49 [reply] ------- ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "CAUSE:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "------\nThis is caused by a badly-populated fedora.fcfg at install-time.  Due to the use",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "of different case when auto-populating the initial fedora.fcfg, the installer",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "ends up creating a partially-populated \"datastore\" element named",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "\"localPostgresqlPool\" (vs. \"localPostgreSQLPool\").  This ultimately causes the",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "NumberFormatException at startup because the ConnectionPoolManager module",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "expects a numeric param value that isn't present for \"localPostgresqlPool\".",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "WORKAROUND:",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "-----------\nUsers can work around this problem by taking the following steps:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "1) After running the installer, open the file",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "$FEDORA_HOME/server/config/fedora.fcfg in an editor.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "2) Find the datastore with id=\"localPostgreSQLPool\" (uppercase SQL).",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "3) Copy all \"param\" elements EXCEPT the first four (dbUsername, dbPassword,",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "jdbcURL, jdbcDriverClass)",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "4) Go to the end of the file, into the datastore with id=\"localPostgresqlPool\"",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "(lowercase sql) and paste the copied \"param\" elements after the four existing",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "elements.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "5) You can now remove the entire, old datastore element with",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "id=\"localPostgreSQLPool\" (uppercase SQL).",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "6) Save the modified fedora.fcfg.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "7) Start Fedora as usual.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
